export interface RateSummary {
  falseAlarm: number;
  missedDetection: number;
}

export class BinaryRateLedger {
  add(falseAlarm: number, missedDetection: number): void;
  average(): RateSummary | null;
  worst(): RateSummary | null;
  reset(): void;
  get size(): number;
}
```

Each rate must be finite and within the inclusive range 0 through 1; otherwise `add` throws `RangeError` and stores neither value. `average` returns arithmetic means. `worst` returns the independent maximum of each field, even if the maxima came from different additions. Both queries return `null` when empty and otherwise return fresh objects. `reset` empties the ledger, and `size` counts additions. Preserve full number precision and do not expose mutable internal storage.

